From 4c284454c9b76706009cde2622bfd52938cff51d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt DeVillier <matt.devillier@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 15:07:23 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] soc/intel/lockdown: Allow locking down SPI and LPC in SMM
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Heads uses APM_CNT_FINALIZE to set and lock the SPI controller with PR0
flash protection. Add SOC_INTEL_COMMON_SPI_LPC_LOCKDOWN_SMM so coreboot
skips SPI/LPC BIOS lockdown in ramstage and applies it from the
APM_CNT_FINALIZE SMI handler instead. When that option is selected,
coreboot also skips issuing APM_CNT_FINALIZE on the normal boot path
(still issues it on S3 resume, where the payload does not run).

This feature is load-bearing for Heads: without it coreboot locks SPI at
BS_DEV_RESOURCES during ramstage, which breaks Heads flashprog/flashrom
firmware updates and hardware reflash, because Heads runs as payload and
needs SPI to remain software-writable.

Carried downstream to coreboot 26.09 by Heads; this feature is not
present in any coreboot release (25.09, 25.12, 26.03, 26.06, 26.09) nor
in current upstream main.  Taken verbatim from upstream Gerrit change
85278 (https://review.coreboot.org/c/coreboot/+/85278), patchset 4,
commit b5ea6e76248f0538b064703eec25a815515cf70d.  The only local
reconciliation is in src/soc/intel/denverton_ns/lpc.c, where 26.09 adds
an extra #include <pc80/i8259.h> that shifts the include block context.

Change-Id: Icbcc6fcde90e5b0a999aacb720e2e3dc2748c838
Co-authored-by: Michał Żygowski <michal.zygowski@3mdeb.com>
Signed-off-by: Matt DeVillier <matt.devillier@gmail.com>
